<title>UK: Molins buys Langen units for 23.1 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Molins buys Langen units for 23.1 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Molins Plc said it has bought the businesses of H J Langen Inc in Canada and Langenpac NV in the Netherlands for a total consideration of some 23.1 million stg in cash and new Molins shares.  </p>
<p>Of the total consideration, 2.2 million stg will be met by the issue of 221,844 new shares in Molins and the balance will be paid in cash from Molins' own resources.</p>
<p>Molins said Langens designs and manufactures a range of cartoning and case packing machines. It employs a total of 200 people in Canada and the Netherlands and key managers will remain with the business.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
